nd in the last few years  it's overwhelmingly two people from  China last year the government gave out  just over 10,000 visas and eighty-five  percent of them were two people from  China alright so this eb-5 program is  being used in connection with a trump  project in jersey tell us about the  project and the extent to which this  program is being  used for so a few years ago I think  about five or six years ago a developer  license the Trump name and built a  high-rise luxury condominium development  called Trump Plaza residents there in  Jersey City it's right on the water it  has incredible views of lower Manhattan  and two years ago jared kushner who is  the CEO of Kushner companies and is  married to donald trump's daughter  Ivanka announced that they would  essentially be building the sister  property a nearly identical 50-story  tower that will actually be luxury  rentals and this is going to be called  Trump Bay Street now typically Donald  Trump for the last 25 years you know has  actually developed and built very few  buildings he has built some but for the  most part his real estate business is a  business of licensing his name to other  developers this is some version of that  we don't exactly know what the financial  arrangement is between him and his  son-in-law but his son-in-law is using  the Trump name on the building that he  is building the financing for the  project a quarter of the financing about  50 million dollars is coming from the  eb-5 visa program in other words the in  other words the cushion her team went  out and found a hundred people I believe  they are almost entirely from China who  each put in half a million dollars and  essentially provided 50 million dollars  in loans to help build this building so  you said I think you just said it's  about a quarter of the financing of the  building given the politics of it why  take the money from China is it is this  the only place that this project can  find enough investment to be to build  well that's a really interesting  question them and I think one of the  reasons that the program is very popular  is because it's basically free money the  investors don't really want a return on  their investment they want the green  card and so where you might have to buy  a borrower from a bank for six percent  or eight percent or ten percent with  these investors you can essentially give  them no return so essentially it's like  getting a quarter of your financing for  no return now the reason the program is  of interest is both the Department of  Homeland Security and the GAO have  raised questions and concerns about the  inadequacy of the screening process for  figuring out where this money is from  and there are concerns that the program  enables money laundering and  jeopardize national security and there  two years ago I believe there was an  internal Department of Homeland Security  memo that Senator Charles Grassley read  on the Senate floor that raised these  very questions just a few months ago the  GAO followed up with another report  raising a similar question but just  because we got to go in a second we said  in beginning there's nothing illegal  obviously about this program and  although the optics from a political  point of view might be bad Trump could  argue right this is just good business  he's getting investment for a project  with his son-in-law that doesn't require  anything much from them and doesn't have  to pay the same rate of return as a  normal investor that's true he's raised  but he's raising money through a  government program that that basically  all government overseers of you is very  troubled and could be enabling a lot of  dirty money to enter the country
 

